-# BossRaceCreator
-BossRaceCreator OSRS plugin+# Boss Race Creator
+
+Boss Race Creator is a RuneLite external plugin scaffold for setting up a simple boss kill-count race reminder. It lets a player configure the race name, boss/activity, target KC, and comma-separated competitors, then announces the configured race in the in-game chat after login.
+
+This repo is prepared as an independent RuneLite plugin project under `/opt/data/HeRmEz/projects/osrs-plugins/BossRaceCreator`.
+
+## Current feature set
+
+- RuneLite plugin entry point: `com.itmeansbigmountain.bossracecreator.BossRaceCreatorPlugin`
+- Config group: `bossracecreator`
+- Configurable race label, boss name, target kill count, competitor list, and login announcement toggle
+- Lightweight local formatting/parsing tests that do not require a live RuneLite client
+- `run` Gradle task for manual RuneLite developer-mode testing
+
+## Configuration
+
+Open RuneLite's plugin configuration panel after loading the plugin and set:
+
+| Setting | Purpose | Default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Race name | Display label for the race | `Clan boss race` |
+| Boss name | Boss/activity to race | `Zulrah` |
+| Target kills | Kill-count target needed to win | `100` |
+| Competitors | Comma-separated player or clan names | blank |
+| Announce on login | Sends the race summary to game chat on login | enabled |
+
+Example announcement:
+
+```text
+Clan boss race: first to 100 Zulrah KC. Competitors: Oyama, Rival.
+```
+
+## API usage notes
+
+The current version does not call Wise Old Man, TempleOSRS, RuneLite hiscores, or any other external API. It is intentionally a low-risk manual race setup/reminder. Future live KC tracking should use background requests, caching, and graceful failure messaging so the RuneLite game thread is never blocked.
+
+## Build and test
+
+Use Java 11 for RuneLite compatibility:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+## Manual RuneLite test plan
+
+1. Start the plugin in developer mode:
+
+   ```bash
+   export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+   ./gradlew run --no-daemon
+   ```
+
+2. Confirm `Boss Race Creator` appears in RuneLite's plugin list.
+3. Open the plugin config panel and edit the race name, boss name, target KC, competitors, and login announcement toggle.
+4. Log into a test account and confirm the chat announcement matches the configured values.
+5. Disable `Announce on login`, relog, and confirm no announcement is sent.
+
+## Plugin Hub prep checklist
+
+Before submitting to `runelite/plugin-hub`:
+
+- Capture a screenshot/GIF of the config panel and chat announcement.
+- Decide whether the first public version should remain manual-only or add live KC lookups.
+- Re-run `./gradlew test --no-daemon -q` and `./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q` on a clean checkout.
+- Verify `runelite-plugin.properties` support URL points to the final public GitHub repo.
